From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serg987 <50438876+serg987@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a527: cubie-a5e: Add CPU thermal backstop

With CPU DVFS enabled, the SoC thermal zones are not enough to keep a
fanless Cubie A5E alive under sustained all-core load. Cooling is only
bound to the 90 C trip, with step_wise and no lower limit, so the
cooling state wanders between 0 and 2 while the die keeps heating. With
stress-ng --cpu 8 and no fan the die reached 108 C and the board shut
down near the 110 C critical trip.

Add two passive trips to both CPU zones that act as hard floors:
- 95 C: both clusters at cooling state 4 or deeper
  (little 1008 MHz, big 1344 MHz with speed bin 0)
- 100 C: both clusters forced to the lowest OPP (408 MHz)

Both clusters are throttled from either sensor because they share the
die. Fanless, 10 minutes of stress-ng --cpu 8 now peaks at 96/98 C with
the 95 C floor engaged and the board stays up. With a fan neither trip
is reached.

Signed-off-by: serg987 <50438876+serg987@users.noreply.github.com>
---

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts
@@ -674,3 +674,70 @@
 &i2s2 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * Thermal backstop for DVFS. The SoC zones only bind cooling to the 90 C
+ * trip (step_wise, no lower limit), which does not hold a fanless board
+ * under sustained all-core load. Add hard floors: at 95 C both clusters
+ * are limited to cooling state 4 or deeper, at 100 C they are forced to
+ * the lowest OPP. Both clusters are throttled from either sensor because
+ * they share the die. Cooling states assume the speed bin 0 OPP tables
+ * (little 0..8, big 0..9).
+ */
+&{/thermal-zones/cpu0-thermal} {
+	trips {
+		cpu0_hot95: cpu-trip-3 {
+			temperature = <95000>;
+			hysteresis = <2000>;
+			type = "passive";
+		};
+
+		cpu0_hot100: cpu-trip-4 {
+			temperature = <100000>;
+			hysteresis = <2000>;
+			type = "passive";
+		};
+	};
+
+	cooling-maps {
+		map-hot95 {
+			trip = <&cpu0_hot95>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu0 4 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+					 <&cpu4 4 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+		};
+
+		map-hot100 {
+			trip = <&cpu0_hot100>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu0 8 8>, <&cpu4 9 9>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&{/thermal-zones/cpu4-thermal} {
+	trips {
+		cpu4_hot95: cpu-trip-3 {
+			temperature = <95000>;
+			hysteresis = <2000>;
+			type = "passive";
+		};
+
+		cpu4_hot100: cpu-trip-4 {
+			temperature = <100000>;
+			hysteresis = <2000>;
+			type = "passive";
+		};
+	};
+
+	cooling-maps {
+		map-hot95 {
+			trip = <&cpu4_hot95>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu0 4 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+					 <&cpu4 4 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+		};
+
+		map-hot100 {
+			trip = <&cpu4_hot100>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu0 8 8>, <&cpu4 9 9>;
+		};
+	};
+};
-- 
